---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ImmersiveInnerHero from './ImmersiveInnerHero.astro';
import AboutRedesignClosing from './AboutRedesignClosing.astro';
import PentaVisual from './PentaVisual.astro';
import {siteImage} from '../data/siteImages';
import '../styles/about-approved.css';
import '../styles/about-constitution.css';
import '../styles/content-image-led.css';
const stages=[
 {id:'quotation-scope',aliases:['ww-define-title','section-3'],title:'Drawing review',buyer:'For a quote, the starting package is a controlled drawing and model with part number, units and revision, plus material, quantity, function and required arrival. For an existing sample, identify the features to retain or change and any measurement or drawing work needed.',lzz:'We check geometry, workholding, cutter access and critical features, raise any questions and propose a machining route or alternatives.',record:'File conflicts need a named controlling document. Geometry or setup changes and permitted alternatives need your approval before production.',href:'/resources/ordering/rfq-checklist/',link:'Prepare the drawing package'},
 {id:'quotation-stage',aliases:['section-4'],title:'Quotation',buyer:'The quotation needs the finish, inspection, sampling and records required, plus the destination and shipping basis.',lzz:'Our quotation sets out the process, material, finish and quantity, together with inspection, records, the production schedule and shipping basis.',record:'The accepted quote records included work, separate charges, payment stages and sample costs alongside the drawing revision.',href:'/resources/ordering/compare-cnc-machining-quotations/',link:'Compare quotation scope'},
 {id:'section-5',aliases:['ww-approval-title'],title:'Sample approval',buyer:'The evaluation needs fit and appearance criteria and any functional test procedure. It also names who supplies mating components and fixtures, who performs the checks and who approves the result.',lzz:'We make the sample to the agreed revision, material and finish, then check it within the evaluation scope. The record keeps approved alternatives and unresolved differences visible.',record:'Approval records the tested configuration, first-article results and release criteria. A substitute prototype material or finish limits what the result establishes. Changes to design, material, finish or route may need fresh approval; batch release is a separate decision.',href:'/resources/ordering/machined-prototype-approval-checklist/',link:'Use the sample approval checklist'},
 {id:'section-6',aliases:[],title:'Production & inspection',buyer:'The production release identifies the revision, material, finish, critical features, datums, sampling and required records.',lzz:'We work to the approved configuration. Measurement methods, instrument range, available calibration evidence and report format are settled with you before ordering.',record:'The order sets first-article checks, recorded measurements, material traceability and handling of nonconforming parts. It also specifies sampling, any 100% inspection, and the calibration records and reports required for CMM measurements.',href:null,link:null},
 {id:'packaging-shipping',aliases:['ww-handover-title','section-8'],title:'Packing & handover',buyer:'Destination, receiving contact, required arrival and handling limits guide the shipment. The packing instructions identify cosmetic faces, seals, threads and fragile edges, with cleanliness, corrosion protection and labels where required.',lzz:'We provide protective packing, a packing list, commercial invoice and shipment information. Material, finishing and dimensional records are included when agreed in the order.',record:'The packing plan covers cartons or wooden cases, separation, pack weight and handling. Labels and packing lists use matching part, revision, batch and quantity references. Transport responsibilities and destination documents are settled before production.',href:'/resources/ordering/custom-cnc-parts-shipping-checklist/',link:'Plan packing and international shipping'},
];
const stageImages=[
 siteImage('home-drawing-review'),
 siteImage('guide-quotations'),
 siteImage('guide-sample-approval'),
 siteImage('home-inspection'),
 siteImage('guide-packing'),
];
---
<Layout title="How we work: drawing review to CNC parts delivery" description="Follow LZZ's order process: drawing review, quotation, sample approval, production, inspection, packing and delivery responsibilities." cta={false}>
 <article class="ar-page ar-workflow rd-wrap rd-page">
  <ImmersiveInnerHero title="From drawing review to finished parts" lead="How we review your drawing, agree the quote and manage machining, inspection and delivery." secondaryHref="#quotation-scope" secondaryLabel="Explore the five stages"/>
  <div class="ar-process-journey"><div class="ar-process-inner">
   <section class="ar-process-opening" data-core-section="Order basis and five stages">
    <dl class="ar-order-basis" id="ww-before-title"><div><dt>Minimum order</dt><dd>From 1 piece</dd></div><div><dt>Production</dt><dd>7-14 business days<p>After drawing and order confirmation, including surface finishing. Transit time is additional.</p></dd></div><div><dt>Payment &amp; samples</dt><dd>Agreed in the quotation<a href="#commercial-terms">Review charges and payment terms</a></dd></div></dl>
   </section>
   <nav class="ar-process-jumps" aria-label="Order stages">{stages.map((stage,index)=><a href={'#'+stage.id}>{index+1}. {stage.title}</a>)}</nav>
   <section class="ar-responsibility-chapter" data-core-section="Buyer, LZZ and release responsibilities"><header><h2>How your order moves forward</h2><p>We confirm the drawing requirements at the start, then agree the checks and approvals needed as the order progresses.</p></header>
    <div class="ar-process-stages">{stages.map((stage,index)=><section class="ar-process-stage" id={stage.id} aria-labelledby={'process-stage-'+index}>
     {stage.aliases.map(id=><span class="ar-anchor" id={id}/>)}
     <span class="ar-process-number" aria-hidden="true">{String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><header class="ar-process-stage-heading"><h3 id={'process-stage-'+index}>{stage.title}</h3></header>
     <PentaVisual class="ar-process-visual" image={stageImages[index]} sizes="(max-width:767px) calc(100vw - 40px), 490px"/>
     <div class="ar-process-responsibilities"><dl><div><dt>What we need from you</dt><dd>{stage.buyer}</dd></div><div><dt>What we do</dt><dd>{stage.lzz}</dd></div><div><dt>Before the next stage</dt><dd>{stage.record}</dd></div></dl>{stage.href&&<a href={stage.href}>{stage.link}</a>}</div>
    </section>)}</div>
   </section>
  </div></div>
  <section class="rd-section ar-order-conditions" aria-labelledby="order-conditions-title" data-core-section="Commercial terms, changes and support">
  <section class="ar-terms" id="commercial-terms"><header><h2 id="order-conditions-title">Commercial terms and delivery</h2><p>The accepted quotation records the price, payment stages and delivery responsibilities.</p></header><dl><div><dt>Price and separate charges</dt><dd>Identify tooling, special documentation, freight and duties where charged separately. Confirm the payment method, currency, payment stages and amount at each stage.</dd></div><div><dt>Sample costs</dt><dd>The quote lists machining, setup and freight charges and any sample-fee credit toward a later order.</dd></div><div><dt>Delivery responsibilities</dt><dd>Distinguish dispatch from arrival. Agree the Incoterm and version, named place, booking, customs clearance, duties, taxes, insurance and local delivery responsibilities. EXW, FOB or DDP applies as quoted; DDP is not automatic.</dd></div><div><dt>Transport and records</dt><dd>Courier, air or sea depends on size and destination; DHL, FedEx or UPS can be discussed. Confirm destination-specific documents before production.</dd></div></dl></section>
  <section class="ar-terms ar-after-sales" id="section-2"><span id="ww-issue-title"/><header><h3>Changes and after-sales</h3></header><dl><div><dt>Changes after approval</dt><dd>A drawing or quantity change can affect price, route and schedule. Review changed features and update the scope; a revised drawing may need sample approval again. <a href="/resources/ordering/prototype-vs-small-batch-cnc/">Plan prototypes and repeat orders</a>.</dd></div><div><dt>Report a nonconforming part</dt><dd>Send the revision, part or batch reference, affected quantity, photographs and measurements. LZZ reviews the discrepancy against the agreed acceptance criteria and agrees corrective action with you.</dd></div><div><dt>Agree the remedy</dt><dd>The order sets warranty coverage, period and start date, exclusions and the reporting procedure, with responsibility for rework, replacement, return freight and any refund. <a href="/about/contact/">Discuss a part discrepancy</a>.</dd></div></dl></section>
  </section>
  <AboutRedesignClosing core="First part inquiry" title="Send us your part requirements" text="Send the current drawing and tell us what still needs to be decided."/>
 </article>
</Layout>

